From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:15:52 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 69/79] flashnext_mia: tool_choice required, a named function
 and Anthropic any force a call (ported from MiaAI-Lab patch 0007)

The lane engine has no grammar hook (and TP2 serves without structures), so checkFeatures refused these with a 400.
Ported from MiaAI-Lab patch 0007: a host-side call gate. Outside a think block, a non-blank answer token is
replaced by the call opener and the lead after it is forced; the name is completed to an offered name and its tail;
a think block the reply opens disarms the gate until it closes. Rank 1 follows rank 0's corrected tokens.

lanes/call_gate.zig holds the gate (Spec, Gate, first, correct). Each stream with Spec.call checks its first
token at the three draw sites (open, open_first, join_batch) and every verify window (gated streams run windowed,
as grammars do); round_cut.zig weighs the gate's cut against the loop guard and the budget (moved out of
engine.zig). The server reads the call form from a probe render of the template (server/tool_call_gate.zig) and
gates only when the backend declares call_gates (flashnext_mia) and has no structures. auto and none are
unchanged; the runner and hold_eos stay off for a gated request, as for a grammar.

Tests (test-call-gate-host): the gate's steps (her two tests among them), and the server's gate for required,
named and any on the chat, responses and messages routes; auto and none get no gate; an engine witness forces
the call from a plain, a thinking and a pipelined reply, and leaves a model's own call byte for byte.
